2026-10-23T18:10:00Z  CHANGE   build.sh: Qt resolution rewritten. Order is environment CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH, newest $HOME/Qt/*/macos (sort -Vr), MacPorts (/opt/local/libexec/qt6), Homebrew, distro, and .qt-stitch LAST. A candidate must contain lib/cmake/Qt6/Qt6Config.cmake -- `-d` cannot tell a prefix from a stale prefix, which is how build-fast ended up on a stitched tree with missing QtGui headers.
2026-10-23T18:10:00Z  CHANGE   build.sh: qt_prefix_changed() parks a build directory that belongs to a different Qt installation (archive_build_dir -> .backup_graveyard/) and configures fresh, because a different installation is not a moved prefix: the objects were built against other headers and the cache carries feature values the new Qt contradicts (Qt warns about exactly that and advises removing CMakeCache.txt). qt_is_stale() keeps the narrower in-place reconfigure for a cached prefix that has merely lost its Qt6Config.cmake.
2026-10-23T18:10:00Z  CHANGE   scripts/qt-stitch.sh moved to .backup_graveyard/qt-stitch.sh.<stamp> and deleted from the tree; .qt-stitch/ parked the same way. docs/dev/TESTING.md loses the stitch instructions and the `--qt "$PWD/.qt-stitch"` lines, and gains the current Qt story (qt.io SDK at $HOME/Qt, CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH from the shell) plus the two-case cache rule.
2026-10-23T18:10:00Z  CHANGE   cmake/Dependencies.cmake: a prefix that carries Qt's own CMake config is excluded from the libav* manual search via CMAKE_IGNORE_PREFIX_PATH (3.23+). Measured in a FRESH build directory: FFMPEG_AVCODEC_INCLUDE_DIR=/usr/local/include paired with FFMPEG_AVCODEC_LIBRARY=~/Qt/6.12.0/macos/lib/libavcodec.dylib -- this tree's 9.x headers against Qt's bundled FFmpeg. The stale cache hid it, which is why only a fresh configure showed it.
2026-10-23T18:24:00Z  CHANGE   tests/CMakeLists.txt: CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH gets ${QT6_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib before add_subdirectory. Test binaries are bare executables, macdeployqt never touches them, and the root sets CMAKE_BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH ON -- so with no entry they carried NO LC_RPATH. Homebrew's frameworks have absolute install names and resolved anyway; qt.io's are @rpath/... and every test died at launch: "Library not loaded: @rpath/QtTest.framework/Versions/A/QtTest ... Reason: no LC_RPATH's found". Measured with ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests -R '^unit_tests$' -V, exit 8 in 6.37 s.
2026-10-23T18:24:00Z  CHANGE   cmake/TargetSetup.cmake: the same missing rpath breaks the BUILD-TREE .app in the fast-iteration profile, because deployment is suppressed so Contents/Frameworks does not exist. INSTALL_RPATH gains ${QT6_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib in that profile only; a shipped bundle keeps @executable_path/../Frameworks and no developer Qt path.
