2026-10-23T19:32:00Z  VERIFY   stale-cache path: build-fast was configured against .qt-stitch. build.sh reported "the Qt this build was configured against (...) is gone or has no Qt6Config.cmake" / "belongs to a different Qt installation" and configured a working directory, after which `./build.sh --fast --tests` reached exit 0 (247 targets) with no --qt flag. That is the item's own acceptance bar: configure without --qt.
2026-10-23T19:32:00Z  VERIFY   rpath: `otool -l build-fast/tests/unit/unit_tests` -> LC_RPATH /Users/derekvanee/Qt/6.12.0/macos/lib (was absent: ctest aborted in 6.37 s with "no LC_RPATH's found"). `otool -l build-fast/chadvis-projectm-qt.app/Contents/MacOS/chadvis-projectm-qt` -> @executable_path/../Frameworks AND the Qt lib dir (fast-iteration only). TestVersion::binaryReportsVersionTxt, which launches the bundle, went from CrashExit to passing.
